        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Computes the output :cpp:class:<computeroutput><ref refid="classONNX__LIGHT__NAMESPACE_1_1onnx__optim_1_1OptimTensor" kindref="compound">OptimTensor</ref></computeroutput> of an <computeroutput>Adam</computeroutput> node and stores it in <computeroutput>ctx</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><computeroutput>Adam</computeroutput> (<computeroutput>ai.onnx.preview.training</computeroutput>) updates <computeroutput>N</computeroutput> optimised tensors and their accumulated first / second moments. The input list has the shape <computeroutput>[R, T, X_1, ..., X_N, G_1, ..., G_N, V_1, ..., V_N, H_1, ..., H_N]</computeroutput> (so <computeroutput>input_size == 2 + 4 * N</computeroutput>) and the output list has the shape <computeroutput>[X_1_new, ..., X_N_new, V_1_new, ..., V_N_new, H_1_new, ..., H_N_new]</computeroutput> (so <computeroutput>output_size == 3 * N</computeroutput>).</para>
<para>Each <computeroutput>*_new</computeroutput> output mirrors the dtype and shape of the corresponding <computeroutput>X_i</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>V_i</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>H_i</computeroutput> input.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ctx</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>In/out context. Must already contain entries for every <computeroutput>X_i</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>V_i</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>H_i</computeroutput> input read from <computeroutput>node</computeroutput>; on return it also contains an entry for every output of <computeroutput>node</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>node</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The <computeroutput>Adam</computeroutput> <computeroutput><ref refid="classONNX__LIGHT__NAMESPACE_1_1NodeProto" kindref="compound">NodeProto</ref></computeroutput> whose outputs should be described. <computeroutput>node.op_type()</computeroutput> must be <computeroutput>&quot;Adam&quot;</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>node.input_size()</computeroutput> must be <computeroutput>2 + 4 * N</computeroutput> for some <computeroutput>N &gt;= 1</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>node.output_size()</computeroutput> must be <computeroutput>3 * N</computeroutput>.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::invalid_argument</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>if <computeroutput>node.op_type()</computeroutput> is not <computeroutput>&quot;Adam&quot;</computeroutput>, if <computeroutput>node</computeroutput> has no output, if the input count minus two is not a positive multiple of four, or if the output count does not match three times the number of optimised tensors. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::out_of_range</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>if any input read from <computeroutput>node</computeroutput> is not present in <computeroutput>ctx</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
